WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.100
Every email is grounded and
approved by a second person.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.033
Now the same rules govern your website.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:09.067
One engine audits your pages, watches
what AI answers say about you,

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:12.867
and ships the fixes. A person
approves every change to your site.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.667
By the end you'll read the
audits and the visibility views,

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:19.000
turn keywords into briefs, and
queue a publish you can undo.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.833
Search Console is required for this
engine, and for this engine only.

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:26.200
Mia's team publishes, then
guesses. Which pages slipped,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.833
which questions the answer engines
now answer without citing you,

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:32.100
which two posts compete for one query.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.233
Search and AI answers are two surfaces.
Nobody has time to watch both.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.367
First, the audit.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:41.967
Tracked pages are audited daily:
crawl, on page checks, schema,

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:46.200
GEO readiness, and the indexed
verdict from Google's URL inspection.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.000
Findings land in the Fix queue, ranked.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.000
In the console: Engines, SEO
and GEO, Pages and Fix queue.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.567
Or ask your agent: "What
is in the fix queue? "

00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:58.300
Second, visibility.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.967
GEO tracks the prompts you care
about across the main answer engines.

00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:05.067
It records who gets cited,
your domain or a competitor.

00:01:05.067 --> 00:01:06.933
Alerts fire when that changes.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:10.500
GEO readiness scores whether
a page is built to be quoted.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.833
Where data is missing, the tile
says why instead of showing a zero.

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:17.967
In the console: the
Visibility and GEO tabs.

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:20.967
Or ask your agent: "How
visible are we in AI answers? "

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.267
Third, keywords.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:24.367
They come from Search
Console queries where

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.067
you already rank just below the top,

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.067
plus looot and Ahrefs
when you connect them.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.767
Search Console is the one connection
this engine can't run without.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:35.167
Connect it once under
Settings, Connected accounts,

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.667
and gtm doctor flags it if it's missing.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.567
Or ask your agent: "Which
keywords are close to page one? "

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.400
Clusters group keywords by
the search results they share.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.567
Two queries that return the
same pages belong to one topic.

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:50.200
Each cluster gets an intent, a
funnel stage and a pillar candidate,

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.733
and shows coverage as
covered, weak or a gap.

00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:57.100
It also flags cannibalization: two of
your pages competing for one topic.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.800
Ask your agent: "Build topic clusters".

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:01.333
Fourth, the content factory.

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:05.167
An idea becomes a brief, a draft,
a quality check and an approval.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.967
Pro move: brief per
cluster, not per keyword,

00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:12.533
so your own posts never compete.
The claims gate runs on the draft.

00:02:12.533 --> 00:02:15.700
Every statistic, result or named
customer must match active proof,

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.933
and a customer whose proof
isn't public is never named.

00:02:18.933 --> 00:02:22.400
Ask your agent: "Draft the
brief for the pricing cluster".

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:24.700
Now the publish, which is a proposal.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:28.267
In the console: Engines, SEO and
GEO, Publish queue, then Approvals.

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:32.267
The change you approve is bound to the
exact payload, the body of the draft,

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.833
so what goes live is what you read.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:37.567
The claims gate and brand safety
run again when it's published.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.600
A publish can be undone, and
the undo is a proposal too.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.967
It reaches your site through a signed
webhook or a connected content system.

00:02:44.967 --> 00:02:47.667
In Dry Mode it stays a logged
draft. Or ask your agent:

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:51.433
"Propose publishing the approved
draft for the pricing cluster".

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:55.367
Content doesn't stay good. In the
console: the Refresh calendar.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:59.967
A page is refresh due when clicks fall,
rank drops, an AI citation is lost,

00:02:59.967 --> 00:03:02.467
or the page ages. You set the thresholds.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.867
A daily watch agent reads the results

00:03:04.867 --> 00:03:07.533
each morning and tells you what changed.

00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:10.133
Or ask your agent: "Which
pages need a refresh? "

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.300
Now the dashboard.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:15.600
The overview shows organic clicks,
average position, GEO readiness,

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.767
tracked pages, AI share of
voice and citation rate.

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:22.067
It also credits visits from
AI assistants to this engine.

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.867
A tile with no data gives the reason.

00:03:24.867 --> 00:03:28.000
Or ask: "How is SEO and
GEO doing this month? "

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.433
It improves from results.

00:03:29.433 --> 00:03:32.833
A page that loses clicks or a
citation becomes refresh due.

00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:35.900
The content refresh play turns
it into a brief and a task.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.700
To customize, set your
tracked pages and prompts,

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.800
the Search Console property, the
content target, refresh thresholds,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:43.400
voice and proof.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.767
Edits to any of these go through a
ChangeSet that a different person signs.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.900
SEO and GEO leans on the proof
library and the claims gate.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.700
It hands briefs to Studio
and the content refresh play,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.633
and it credits visits from AI answers
to this engine in attribution.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.700
The honest edge, built or not. Publishing
straight to Webflow or WordPress.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.000
com hasn't been tested
against real accounts.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.633
Treat it as optional and
try a staging site first.

00:04:06.633 --> 00:04:10.833
Automatic fixes for gaps in AI answers,
and a link graph, aren't built yet.

00:04:10.867 --> 00:04:14.533
The objection: an agent that can
publish to my site is a liability.

00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:15.767
It can't publish alone.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:18.433
A publish is a proposal that
a different person approves.

00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:20.567
The approval is bound
to the exact payload,

00:04:20.567 --> 00:04:23.100
and the claims gate runs
again when it's published.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.933
If the proof expires in
between, the publish fails.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.200
Keep these: Audit daily,
track what AI answers cite,

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.667
and draft behind a claims gate.

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:34.367
What goes live is what you
approved, and you can take it back.

00:04:34.433 --> 00:04:37.700
Your pages are audited daily,
your AI visibility is tracked,

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:40.833
and every publish is checked,
approved and undoable.

00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:43.033
Read the top three items in the Fix queue.

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:46.933
The next clip is Performance ads,
where the same rule guards your budget.
